{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8iKFJVEpsVfBHPeFMhrvQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 被证伪或效应不泛化。binarized Likert sign test\n2\t  显著 (p<0.04) 证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 来自统计检验功效差异而非测量方法结构性优势；或者效应仅限 GPT-4o × LLMBar，Claude/Gemini\n3\t  均不显著，additional benchmarks 不复制。需要根本性 reframe：路径 A (sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs)\n4\t  或路径 B (original-text preference confound as cautionary negative result)。C4 在此 tier\n5\t  反而更重要——\"what NOT to do\" 本身就是贡献。目标仍为 EMNLP Findings (projected 2.8-3.3)。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n10\t  plan_id: exp-001\n11\t  description: '在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n12\t    使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\n13\t\n14\t    '\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n17\t    gpt4o_sign_p: 0.006\n18\t    claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n19\t    claude_sign_p: 0.42\n20\t    claude_n_consistent: 44\n21\t    claude_formal_wins: 24\n22\t    claude_casual_wins: 20\n23\t    gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n24\t    gemini_sign_p: 0.68\n25\t    gemini_n_consistent: 48\n26\t    gemini_formal_wins: 25\n27\t    gemini_casual_wins: 23\n28\t    n_judges_pairwise_significant: 1\n29\t    cross_judge_formal_win_rate: 0.552\n30\t    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.42\n31\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal\n32\t    bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的 偏好结构不同。GPT-4o\n33\t    的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning 偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured\n34\t    输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用 属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着 \"style\n35\t    bias in LLM judges\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \"GPT-4o exhibits formality preference\n36\t    as a judge\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\n37\t\n38\t    '\n39\t  tables:\n40\t  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results'\n41\t    columns:\n42\t    - Judge\n43\t    - N_consistent\n44\t    - Formal_wins\n45\t    - Casual_wins\n46\t    - Win_rate\n47\t    - Sign_p\n48\t    - Wilson_CI\n49\t    rows:\n50\t    - - GPT-4o\n51\t      - 55\n52\t      - 38\n53\t      - 17\n54\t      - 69.1%\n55\t      - 0.006**\n56\t      - '[0.56, 0.80]'\n57\t    - - Claude-3.5-Sonnet\n58\t      - 44\n59\t      - 24\n60\t      - 20\n61\t      - 54.5%\n62\t      - '0.42'\n63\t      - '[0.40, 0.69]'\n64\t    - - Gemini-2.0-Flash\n65\t      - 48\n66\t      - 25\n67\t      - 23\n68\t      - 52.1%\n69\t      - '0.68'\n70\t      - '[0.38, 0.66]'\n71\t  figures_description:\n72\t  - 'Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 及 95% Wilson CI。GPT-4o CI 不含 50%，Claude\n73\t    和 Gemini CI 宽且跨 50%。视觉上清晰显示效应不泛化。'\n74\t  analysis: '仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右， 但 heterogeneity\n75\t    极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\" — 只能说 \"GPT-4o as judge prefers\n76\t    formal text\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality 和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \"the bias\n77\t    we detect is judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation\n78\t    in bias audits\"。\n79\t\n80\t    '\n81\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n82\t  plan_id: exp-002\n83\t  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。 新 counterfactual\n84\t    generation + 三个 judge 评估。\n85\t\n86\t    '\n87\t  expected_results:\n88\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n89\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.31\n90\t    gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.53\n91\t    gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p: 0.55\n92\t    claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n93\t    claude_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.84\n94\t    claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n95\t    claude_mtbench_sign_p: 0.72\n96\t    gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.5\n97\t    gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.95\n98\t    gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n99\t    gemini_mtbench_sign_p: 0.49\n100\t    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 0\n101\t    nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n102\t    nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.79\n103\t    n_combos_significant_of_6: 0\n104\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的：\n105\t    (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs 有明确的 correct/incorrect\n106\t    之分，formality 在 \"明确有对错\" 的场景下更容易影响 judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response\n107\t    质量差异更大更 noisy， style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布\n108\t    不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse， counterfactual\n109\t    rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual\n110\t    quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。 这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific\n111\t    而非 generalizable。\n112\t\n113\t    '\n114\t  tables:\n115\t  - name: 'Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)'\n116\t    columns:\n117\t    - Judge\n118\t    - Benchmark\n119\t    - N_consistent\n120\t    - Formal_WR\n121\t    - Sign_p\n122\t    rows:\n123\t    - - GPT-4o\n124\t      - LLMBar\n125\t      - 55\n126\t      - 69.1%\n127\t      - 0.006**\n128\t    - - GPT-4o\n129\t      - AlpacaEval\n130\t      - 48\n131\t      - 56.3%\n132\t      - '0.31'\n133\t    - - GPT-4o\n134\t      - MT-Bench\n135\t      - 42\n136\t      - 52.4%\n137\t      - '0.55'\n138\t    - - Claude\n139\t      - LLMBar\n140\t      - 44\n141\t      - 54.5%\n142\t      - '0.42'\n143\t    - - Claude\n144\t      - AlpacaEval\n145\t      - 45\n146\t      - 51.1%\n147\t      - '0.84'\n148\t    - - Claude\n149\t      - MT-Bench\n150\t      - 40\n151\t      - 47.5%\n152\t      - '0.72'\n153\t    - - Gemini\n154\t      - LLMBar\n155\t      - 48\n156\t      - 52.1%\n157\t      - '0.68'\n158\t    - - Gemini\n159\t      - AlpacaEval\n160\t      - 46\n161\t      - 50.0%\n162\t      - '0.95'\n163\t    - - Gemini\n164\t      - MT-Bench\n165\t      - 43\n166\t      - 53.5%\n167\t      - '0.49'\n168\t  figures_description:\n169\t  - 'Heatmap: 3×3 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate，颜色编码偏离 50% 程度。仅左上角 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\n170\t    显著着色，其余接近中性灰。'\n171\t  analysis: '9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后 连这一个也不再显著\n172\t    (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果 formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark\n173\t    交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \"benchmark characteristics mediate\n174\t    bias detectability\"，但说服力有限。\n175\t\n176\t    '\n177\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n178\t  plan_id: exp-003\n179\t  description: '对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t  expected_results:\n183\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n184\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n185\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n186\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n187\t    gpt4o_llmbar_gap: significant\n188\t    claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n189\t    claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n190\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.545\n191\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n192\t    claude_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n193\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n194\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.82\n195\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.521\n196\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.68\n197\t    gemini_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n198\t    n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n199\t    n_combos_both_null: 7\n200\t    n_combos_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n201\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。\n202\t    其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \"gap\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的\n203\t    gap 案例可能是 statistical fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert\n204\t    也 显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献 完全瓦解。\n205\t\n206\t    '\n207\t  tables:\n208\t  - name: 'Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison'\n209\t    columns:\n210\t    - Judge\n211\t    - Benchmark\n212\t    - Likert_ATE\n213\t    - Likert_p\n214\t    - Pairwise_WR\n215\t    - Pairwise_p\n216\t    - Gap\n217\t    rows:\n218\t    - - GPT-4o\n219\t      - LLMBar\n220\t      - '-0.10'\n221\t      - '0.33'\n222\t      - 69.1%\n223\t      - 0.006**\n224\t      - Pairwise-only\n225\t    - - GPT-4o\n226\t      - AlpacaEval\n227\t      - '0.04'\n228\t      - '0.71'\n229\t      - 56.3%\n230\t      - '0.31'\n231\t      - Neither\n232\t    - - GPT-4o\n233\t      - MT-Bench\n234\t      - '0.01'\n235\t      - '0.92'\n236\t      - 52.4%\n237\t      - '0.55'\n238\t      - Neither\n239\t    - - Claude\n240\t      - LLMBar\n241\t      - '0.05'\n242\t      - '0.61'\n243\t      - 54.5%\n244\t      - '0.42'\n245\t      - Neither\n246\t    - - Claude\n247\t      - AlpacaEval\n248\t      - '-0.02'\n249\t      - '0.85'\n250\t      - 51.1%\n251\t      - '0.84'\n252\t      - Neither\n253\t    - - Claude\n254\t      - MT-Bench\n255\t      - '0.03'\n256\t      - '0.77'\n257\t      - 47.5%\n258\t      - '0.72'\n259\t      - Neither\n260\t    - - Gemini\n261\t      - LLMBar\n262\t      - '0.02'\n263\t      - '0.82'\n264\t      - 52.1%\n265\t      - '0.68'\n266\t      - Neither\n267\t    - - Gemini\n268\t      - AlpacaEval\n269\t      - '0.00'\n270\t      - '0.99'\n271\t      - 50.0%\n272\t      - '0.95'\n273\t      - Neither\n274\t    - - Gemini\n275\t      - MT-Bench\n276\t      - '0.06'\n277\t      - '0.55'\n278\t      - 53.5%\n279\t      - '0.49'\n280\t      - Neither\n281\t  figures_description:\n282\t  - 'Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合的 Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value，红线标\n283\t    0.05。仅一个组合的 pairwise 柱低于红线。'\n284\t  analysis: 'C2 的 \"Likert Blindspot\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but pairwise\n285\t    detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被 exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise\n286\t    在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应—— 这更像 \"there is no bias to detect\" 而非 \"Likert misses bias\"。\n287\t\n288\t    '\n289\t- name: Tone axis negative control\n290\t  plan_id: exp-004\n291\t  description: 'Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录 epistemic\n292\t    commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\n293\t\n294\t    '\n295\t  expected_results:\n296\t    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n297\t    both_pass_rate: 0.45\n298\t    failure_mode: epistemic commitment change\n299\t    role_in_paper: negative control — axis boundary evidence\n300\t    assertive_nli_mean: 0.656\n301\t    hedging_nli_mean: 0.793\n302\t    catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n303\t  result_rationale: '此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone 作为 negative\n304\t    control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱： working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而\n305\t    formality 又只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\"\n306\t    不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅 作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t  tables: []\n310\t  figures_description:\n311\t  - 'Method boundary diagram: formality (content-preserving ✅) vs tone (epistemic\n312\t    commitment change ✗) vs verbosity (information-changing ✗)。简单分类图，不需要新数据。'\n313\t  analysis: 'C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\"，\n314\t    贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability window\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\n315\t\n316\t    '\n317\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n318\t  plan_id: exp-005\n319\t  description: 'Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化 original\n320\t    preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n321\t\n322\t    '\n323\t  expected_results:\n324\t    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.62\n325\t    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.048\n326\t    claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n327\t    claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n328\t    gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n329\t    gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.31\n330\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr: 0.59\n331\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p: 0.12\n332\t    gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr: 0.61\n333\t    gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n334\t    cross_condition_orig_pref_mean: 0.59\n335\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n336\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.5\n337\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.48\n338\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge: 0.545\n339\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \"style bias\"。\n340\t    GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好 62%），剩余 formality\n341\t    特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset： 当 original 是 casual（即 formal version\n342\t    是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅 54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality\n343\t    bias 几乎消失。 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)， 在\n344\t    worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset 的 formal win rate\n345\t    在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \"formality bias\" 可能本质上是 \"original text preference + directional\n346\t    confound\"。\n347\t\n348\t    '\n349\t  tables:\n350\t  - name: 'Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)'\n351\t    columns:\n352\t    - Judge\n353\t    - Benchmark\n354\t    - Orig_pref_WR\n355\t    - Orig_pref_p\n356\t    - Casual-orig_formal_WR\n357\t    - Casual-orig_p\n358\t    rows:\n359\t    - - GPT-4o\n360\t      - LLMBar\n361\t      - 62.0%\n362\t      - 0.048*\n363\t      - 54.5%\n364\t      - '0.83'\n365\t    - - GPT-4o\n366\t      - AlpacaEval\n367\t      - 59.0%\n368\t      - '0.12'\n369\t      - 51.2%\n370\t      - '0.91'\n371\t    - - GPT-4o\n372\t      - MT-Bench\n373\t      - 61.0%\n374\t      - '0.06'\n375\t      - 50.0%\n376\t      - '1.00'\n377\t    - - Claude\n378\t      - LLMBar\n379\t      - 58.0%\n380\t      - '0.18'\n381\t      - 50.0%\n382\t      - '1.00'\n383\t    - - Gemini\n384\t      - LLMBar\n385\t      - 56.0%\n386\t      - '0.31'\n387\t      - 48.0%\n388\t      - '0.72'\n389\t  figures_description:\n390\t  - 'Decomposition bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate 分解为 original preference\n391\t    component + residual formality component。视觉上显示 residual 接近 0。'\n392\t  analysis: 'Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual\n393\t    formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\"apparent style bias is confounded with\n394\t    original-text preference\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50% win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality\n395\t    和 original preference 方向相反时， formality bias 消失。\n396\t\n397\t    '\n398\t- name: Scaled replication (n=300-500)\n399\t  plan_id: exp-006\n400\t  description: '将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。 Power analysis\n401\t    确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n402\t\n403\t    '\n404\t  expected_results:\n405\t    n_total: 400\n406\t    n_valid_consistent: 220\n407\t    formal_wins: 132\n408\t    casual_wins: 88\n409\t    formal_win_rate: 0.6\n410\t    sign_p: 0.004\n411\t    wilson_ci:\n412\t    - 0.534\n413\t    - 0.663\n414\t    power_at_d02: 0.35\n415\t    power_at_d05: 0.88\n416\t    casual_orig_subset_n: 95\n417\t    casual_orig_formal_wr: 0.516\n418\t    casual_orig_p: 0.67\n419\t    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n420\t    effect_size_cohens_h: 0.2\n421\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1% 下降到\n422\t    60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original subset 在 n≈95 时 formal\n423\t    win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在 控制 original preference 后消失。effect size\n424\t    (Cohen''s h=0.20) 属于 small， 且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power\n425\t    仅 35%——如果真实 效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了 formality 和 original\n426\t    preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\"at scale, the significant overall effect decomposes into\n427\t    original preference + noise\"。\n428\t\n429\t    '\n430\t  tables:\n431\t  - name: 'Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)'\n432\t    columns:\n433\t    - Subset\n434\t    - N\n435\t    - Formal_WR\n436\t    - Sign_p\n437\t    - 95% CI\n438\t    rows:\n439\t    - - All consistent\n440\t      - 220\n441\t      - 60.0%\n442\t      - 0.004**\n443\t      - '[0.534, 0.663]'\n444\t    - - Formal-original\n445\t      - 125\n446\t      - 66.4%\n447\t      - 0.001**\n448\t      - '[0.577, 0.742]'\n449\t    - - Casual-original\n450\t      - 95\n451\t      - 51.6%\n452\t      - '0.67'\n453\t      - '[0.415, 0.615]'\n454\t    - - NLI≥0.90\n455\t      - 187\n456\t      - 61.5%\n457\t      - 0.003**\n458\t      - '[0.543, 0.683]'\n459\t  figures_description:\n460\t  - Formal win rate 随 n 增长的 running average plot，标 95% CI band。显示效应从 ~69% 向 ~60% 收敛，且\n461\t    casual-original subset 收敛到 ~50%。\n462\t  analysis: 'n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)； (2) casual-original\n463\t    subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \"original preference confound\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\n464\t\n465\t    '\n466\t- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n467\t  plan_id: exp-008\n468\t  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变 词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\n469\t\n470\t    '\n471\t  expected_results:\n472\t    n: 100\n473\t    nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n474\t    bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n475\t    joint_pass_rate: 0.48\n476\t    stopped_at: content_verification\n477\t    stop_reason: NLI 72% < 80% threshold\n478\t    academic_to_conversational_nli_mean: 0.81\n479\t    conversational_to_academic_nli_mean: 0.65\n480\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational\n481\t    转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \"our findings demonstrate\" 变成口语\n482\t    \"we found\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的 \"statistically significant correlation\n483\t    (r=0.82, p<0.001)\" 变成口语 \"there''s a pretty strong link\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic\n484\t    方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers, citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72%\n485\t    总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD 方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\n486\t\n487\t    '\n488\t  tables:\n489\t  - name: 'Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification'\n490\t    columns:\n491\t    - Direction\n492\t    - N\n493\t    - NLI_mean\n494\t    - NLI≥0.80\n495\t    - BERTScore_mean\n496\t    rows:\n497\t    - - Academic→Conversational\n498\t      - 52\n499\t      - '0.81'\n500\t      - 73%\n501\t      - '0.82'\n502\t    - - Conversational→Academic\n503\t      - 48\n504\t      - '0.65'\n505\t      - 52%\n506\t      - '0.77'\n507\t    - - Overall\n508\t      - 100\n509\t      - '0.72'\n510\t      - 63%\n511\t      - '0.80'\n512\t  figures_description: []\n513\t  analysis: 'register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围 收窄到仅 formality——且即使\n514\t    formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。 C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\"we attempted\n515\t    three additional axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\"。\n516\t\n517\t    '\n518\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n519\t  plan_id: exp-009\n520\t  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n521\t\n522\t    '\n523\t  expected_results:\n524\t    llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.8\n525\t    llama_bertscore_mean: 0.88\n526\t    llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.58\n527\t    llama_sign_p: 0.21\n528\t    qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.691\n529\t    qwen_sign_p: 0.006\n530\t    rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.72\n531\t    nli_correlation_qwen_llama: 0.61\n532\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58%\n533\t    (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting style 不同，Llama\n534\t    可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80% vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对\n535\t    rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本 显著。这引入 \"researcher degrees of freedom\" 质疑——如果换一个\n536\t    rewriter 就不 显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个 rewriter\n537\t    的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\n538\t\n539\t    '\n540\t  tables:\n541\t  - name: 'Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check'\n542\t    columns:\n543\t    - Rewriter\n544\t    - NLI_pass\n545\t    - Formal_WR\n546\t    - Sign_p\n547\t    - N_consistent\n548\t    rows:\n549\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n550\t      - 88%\n551\t      - 69.1%\n552\t      - 0.006**\n553\t      - 55\n554\t    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n555\t      - 80%\n556\t      - 58.0%\n557\t      - '0.21'\n558\t      - 50\n559\t  figures_description:\n560\t  - 'Scatter plot: 100 pairs 的 Qwen NLI score vs Llama NLI score，标 0.80 threshold\n561\t    线。显示 moderate correlation 但有 substantial disagreement zone。'\n562\t  analysis: 'rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到 formality\n563\t    bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。 路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\n564\t\n565\t    '\n566\t- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n567\t  plan_id: exp-010\n568\t  description: '对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本， formal\n569\t    version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t  expected_results:\n573\t    n_pairs: 88\n574\t    formal_higher: 42\n575\t    casual_higher: 26\n576\t    tied: 20\n577\t    n_non_tied: 68\n578\t    binarized_sign_p: 0.032\n579\t    formal_higher_rate: 0.618\n580\t    effect_direction: formal preferred in binarized Likert too\n581\t  result_rationale: '这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04，\n582\t    说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33 不显著是因为 Likert\n583\t    评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise 大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise\n584\t    gap 来自 sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对 小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired\n585\t    t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \"Likert Blindspot\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t\n586\t    检验在 粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise） 都能检测到效应。C2 从 \"measurement\n587\t    method structural advantage\" 坍缩为 \"statistical test choice matters\"——这是 trivially\n588\t    true 且 novelty 极低。\n589\t\n590\t    '\n591\t  tables:\n592\t  - name: 'Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison'\n593\t    columns:\n594\t    - Method\n595\t    - N_non-tied\n596\t    - Formal_preferred\n597\t    - Preferred_rate\n598\t    - Sign_test_p\n599\t    rows:\n600\t    - - Likert (paired t-test)\n601\t      - 88\n602\t      - —\n603\t      - —\n604\t      - '0.332'\n605\t    - - Likert (binarized sign test)\n606\t      - 68\n607\t      - 42\n608\t      - 61.8%\n609\t      - 0.032*\n610\t    - - Pairwise (sign test)\n611\t      - 55\n612\t      - 38\n613\t      - 69.1%\n614\t      - 0.006**\n615\t  figures_description:\n616\t  - 三栏对比图：左=Likert paired t-test (NS)，中=Binarized Likert sign test (p=0.032)，右=Pairwise\n617\t    sign test (p=0.006)。视觉化显示 gap 来自 test choice 而非 measurement method。\n618\t  analysis: 'C2 证伪。\"Likert Blindspot\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是： \"Pairwise comparison\n619\t    amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation, but this amplification\n620\t    also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise should be treated as complementary\n621\t    detectors with different sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs。\" 标题改为 \"Sensitivity-Specificity\n622\t    Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias Detection\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\"不同方法有不同检测特性\") 而非 prescriptive\n623\t    (\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\")。\n624\t\n625\t    '\n626\t- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n627\t  plan_id: exp-011\n628\t  description: '测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\n629\t\n630\t    '\n631\t  expected_results:\n632\t    threshold_70_n: 82\n633\t    threshold_70_formal_wr: 0.65\n634\t    threshold_70_p: 0.018\n635\t    threshold_75_n: 75\n636\t    threshold_75_formal_wr: 0.67\n637\t    threshold_75_p: 0.012\n638\t    threshold_80_n: 68\n639\t    threshold_80_formal_wr: 0.68\n640\t    threshold_80_p: 0.009\n641\t    threshold_85_n: 58\n642\t    threshold_85_formal_wr: 0.7\n643\t    threshold_85_p: 0.006\n644\t    threshold_90_n: 46\n645\t    threshold_90_formal_wr: 0.74\n646\t    threshold_90_p: 0.002\n647\t    threshold_95_n: 30\n648\t    threshold_95_formal_wr: 0.77\n649\t    threshold_95_p: 0.005\n650\t    monotonic_increase: true\n651\t    critical_finding: higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\n652\t  result_rationale: '结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是 \"方法 robust\"，而是\n653\t    \"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality 是 confound\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是\n654\t    rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version 更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以\n655\t    judge 偏好 formal version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold\n656\t    70% 时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。 这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但\n657\t    worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否 systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\n658\t\n659\t    '\n660\t  tables:\n661\t  - name: 'Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity'\n662\t    columns:\n663\t    - Threshold\n664\t    - N_consistent\n665\t    - Formal_WR\n666\t    - Sign_p\n667\t    - Cohen's_h\n668\t    rows:\n669\t    - - '0.70'\n670\t      - 60\n671\t      - 65.0%\n672\t      - '0.018'\n673\t      - '0.31'\n674\t    - - '0.75'\n675\t      - 56\n676\t      - 67.0%\n677\t      - '0.012'\n678\t      - '0.35'\n679\t    - - '0.80'\n680\t      - 52\n681\t      - 68.0%\n682\t      - '0.009'\n683\t      - '0.37'\n684\t    - - '0.85'\n685\t      - 46\n686\t      - 70.0%\n687\t      - '0.006'\n688\t      - '0.41'\n689\t    - - '0.90'\n690\t      - 38\n691\t      - 73.7%\n692\t      - '0.002'\n693\t      - '0.49'\n694\t    - - '0.95'\n695\t      - 26\n696\t      - 76.9%\n697\t      - '0.005'\n698\t      - '0.57'\n699\t  figures_description:\n700\t  - 'Dual-axis line chart: x=NLI threshold, left y=formal win rate (上升), right y=n\n701\t    (下降)。显示 sensitivity-sample size tradeoff。'\n702\t  analysis: '结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要 这个实验不显著——它需要的是\n703\t    effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。 路径 B 下这可以作为 \"methodological caveat: NLI\n704\t    filtering may introduce selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\"。\n705\t\n706\t    '\n707\t- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n708\t  plan_id: exp-012\n709\t  description: '比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths,\n710\t    task types。零成本 reanalysis。\n711\t\n712\t    '\n713\t  expected_results:\n714\t    consistent_n: 55\n715\t    inconsistent_n: 43\n716\t    discard_rate: 0.439\n717\t    consistent_mean_nli: 0.91\n718\t    inconsistent_mean_nli: 0.87\n719\t    nli_diff_p: 0.08\n720\t    consistent_mean_orig_len: 285\n721\t    inconsistent_mean_orig_len: 342\n722\t    length_diff_p: 0.03\n723\t    consistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.58\n724\t    inconsistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.51\n725\t    task_type_distribution_differs: true\n726\t    chi2_task_type_p: 0.04\n727\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98)\n728\t    相比 inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)； (2)\n729\t    更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长 (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是\n730\t    task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs 过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained\n731\t    pairs 是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否 仅反映了 filter 保留的特定\n732\t    task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被 formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative\n733\t    salience 更高），那 bias 来自 filtering 而非 formality。\n734\t\n735\t    '\n736\t  tables:\n737\t  - name: 'Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check'\n738\t    columns:\n739\t    - Property\n740\t    - Consistent (n=55)\n741\t    - Inconsistent (n=43)\n742\t    - Diff_p\n743\t    rows:\n744\t    - - NLI mean\n745\t      - '0.91'\n746\t      - '0.87'\n747\t      - '0.08'\n748\t    - - Orig text length (chars)\n749\t      - '285'\n750\t      - '342'\n751\t      - 0.03*\n752\t    - - Formal version longer (%)\n753\t      - 58%\n754\t      - 51%\n755\t      - '0.34'\n756\t    - - Task type χ²\n757\t      - —\n758\t      - —\n759\t      - 0.04*\n760\t  figures_description:\n761\t  - 'Box plots: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI score 和 text length 分布对比。'\n762\t  analysis: 'filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了 \"results\n763\t    may be an artifact of data processing choices\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下 需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity\n764\t    analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求 看效应是否持续)。\n765\t\n766\t    '\n767\t- name: Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\n768\t  plan_id: exp-013\n769\t  description: '人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。 报告 human-NLI\n770\t    Cohen''s kappa。\n771\t\n772\t    '\n773\t  expected_results:\n774\t    n_annotated: 80\n775\t    human_pass_rate: 0.74\n776\t    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n777\t    agreement_rate: 0.78\n778\t    cohens_kappa: 0.42\n779\t    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.18\n780\t    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.08\n781\t    human_agrees_formal_better_preserved: true\n782\t    annotation_method: LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\n783\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false\n784\t    positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs 如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content\n785\t    差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42\n786\t    属于 \"moderate agreement\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline acceptable。GPT-4o\n787\t    作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular\n788\t    validation 风险。20 个 human spot checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\n789\t\n790\t    '\n791\t  tables:\n792\t  - name: 'Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement'\n793\t    columns:\n794\t    - ''\n795\t    - 'Human: Pass'\n796\t    - 'Human: Fail'\n797\t    rows:\n798\t    - - 'NLI: Pass (n=68)'\n799\t      - 56 (TP)\n800\t      - 12 (FP)\n801\t    - - 'NLI: Fail (n=12)'\n802\t      - 3 (FN)\n803\t      - 9 (TN)\n804\t    - - ''\n805\t      - κ = 0.42\n806\t      - ''\n807\t  figures_description: []\n808\t  analysis: 'moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着 ~10 个 consistent\n809\t    pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径\n810\t    B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis excluding human-flagged false positives。\n811\t\n812\t    '\n813\t- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n814\t  plan_id: exp-014\n815\t  description: 'Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction\n816\t    作为 predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\n817\t\n818\t    '\n819\t  expected_results:\n820\t    n_observations: 110\n821\t    model_aic: 142.3\n822\t    model_bic: 153.1\n823\t    formality_coef: 0.28\n824\t    formality_coef_se: 0.22\n825\t    formality_coef_p: 0.21\n826\t    original_status_coef: 0.65\n827\t    original_status_coef_se: 0.21\n828\t    original_status_coef_p: 0.002\n829\t    interaction_coef: 0.12\n830\t    interaction_coef_p: 0.58\n831\t    pseudo_r2: 0.06\n832\t    casual_orig_subset_n: 38\n833\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.526\n834\t    casual_orig_sign_p: 0.72\n835\t    formal_orig_subset_n: 50\n836\t    formal_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.78\n837\t    formal_orig_sign_p: 0.001\n838\t    logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.21\n839\t    logistic_original_status_p: 0.002\n840\t  result_rationale: 'worst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status 显著\n841\t    (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects： (1) formality coefficient\n842\t    p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2)\n843\t    original_status coefficient p=0.002—— 是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明\n844\t    original preference 不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是\n845\t    formal 还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6% (p=0.72)——当\n846\t    formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当\n847\t    formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈 偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo\n848\t    R² = 0.06 说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的 statistical backbone：\"formality\n849\t    bias is an artifact of original-text preference\"。\n850\t\n851\t    '\n852\t  tables:\n853\t  - name: 'Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction'\n854\t    columns:\n855\t    - Predictor\n856\t    - Coefficient\n857\t    - SE\n858\t    - z\n859\t    - p\n860\t    rows:\n861\t    - - Intercept\n862\t      - '-0.42'\n863\t      - '0.31'\n864\t      - '-1.35'\n865\t      - '0.18'\n866\t    - - Formality (formal=1)\n867\t      - '0.28'\n868\t      - '0.22'\n869\t      - '1.27'\n870\t      - '0.21'\n871\t    - - Original status (original=1)\n872\t      - '0.65'\n873\t      - '0.21'\n874\t      - '3.10'\n875\t      - 0.002**\n876\t    - - Formality × Original\n877\t      - '0.12'\n878\t      - '0.22'\n879\t      - '0.55'\n880\t      - '0.58'\n881\t  - name: 'Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status'\n882\t    columns:\n883\t    - Subset\n884\t    - N\n885\t    - Formal_WR\n886\t    - Sign_p\n887\t    - Interpretation\n888\t    rows:\n889\t    - - Formal is original\n890\t      - 50\n891\t      - 78.0%\n892\t      - 0.001**\n893\t      - Original pref + formality aligned\n894\t    - - Casual is original\n895\t      - 38\n896\t      - 52.6%\n897\t      - '0.72'\n898\t      - Original pref opposes formality → null\n899\t    - - Overall\n900\t      - 88\n901\t      - 64.8%\n902\t      - 0.01*\n903\t      - Confounded aggregate\n904\t  figures_description:\n905\t  - 两组 bar chart：左=formal-original subset (78%, 高), 右=casual-original subset (52.6%,\n906\t    平)。视觉化 formality 效应在控制 original status 后消失。\n907\t  - 'Coefficient forest plot: formality (CI 跨 0), original status (CI 不跨 0), interaction\n908\t    (CI 跨 0)。'\n909\t  analysis: 这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的 \"formality bias\"\n910\t    实际上是 \"original text preference\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此： \"Standard bias detection methods\n911\t    that compare original vs style-transferred text confound style preference with\n912\t    original-text preference。Only the casual-original subset provides an unconfounded\n913\t    estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\" C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\"always\n914\t    control for original status in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset\n915\t    analyses by original direction\"。\n916\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c59a25f3-5298-4d00-827e-6615192a7872","uuid":"d2f6aef6-8cf1-42da-a956-521ae06e0eb8","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:31:00.797Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 被证伪或效应不泛化。binarized Likert sign test\n  显著 (p<0.04) 证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 来自统计检验功效差异而非测量方法结构性优势；或者效应仅限 GPT-4o × LLMBar，Claude/Gemini\n  均不显著，additional benchmarks 不复制。需要根本性 reframe：路径 A (sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs)\n  或路径 B (original-text preference confound as cautionary negative result)。C4 在此 tier\n  反而更重要——\"what NOT to do\" 本身就是贡献。目标仍为 EMNLP Findings (projected 2.8-3.3)。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: '在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n    使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n    gpt4o_sign_p: 0.006\n    claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n    claude_sign_p: 0.42\n    claude_n_consistent: 44\n    claude_formal_wins: 24\n    claude_casual_wins: 20\n    gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n    gemini_sign_p: 0.68\n    gemini_n_consistent: 48\n    gemini_formal_wins: 25\n    gemini_casual_wins: 23\n    n_judges_pairwise_significant: 1\n    cross_judge_formal_win_rate: 0.552\n    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.42\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal\n    bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的 偏好结构不同。GPT-4o\n    的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning 偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured\n    输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用 属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着 \"style\n    bias in LLM judges\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \"GPT-4o exhibits formality preference\n    as a judge\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - N_consistent\n    - Formal_wins\n    - Casual_wins\n    - Win_rate\n    - Sign_p\n    - Wilson_CI\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 17\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - '[0.56, 0.80]'\n    - - Claude-3.5-Sonnet\n      - 44\n      - 24\n      - 20\n      - 54.5%\n      - '0.42'\n      - '[0.40, 0.69]'\n    - - Gemini-2.0-Flash\n      - 48\n      - 25\n      - 23\n      - 52.1%\n      - '0.68'\n      - '[0.38, 0.66]'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 及 95% Wilson CI。GPT-4o CI 不含 50%，Claude\n    和 Gemini CI 宽且跨 50%。视觉上清晰显示效应不泛化。'\n  analysis: '仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右， 但 heterogeneity\n    极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\" — 只能说 \"GPT-4o as judge prefers\n    formal text\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality 和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \"the bias\n    we detect is judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation\n    in bias audits\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。 新 counterfactual\n    generation + 三个 judge 评估。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.31\n    gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.53\n    gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p: 0.55\n    claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n    claude_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.84\n    claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n    claude_mtbench_sign_p: 0.72\n    gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.5\n    gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.95\n    gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n    gemini_mtbench_sign_p: 0.49\n    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 0\n    nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n    nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.79\n    n_combos_significant_of_6: 0\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的：\n    (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs 有明确的 correct/incorrect\n    之分，formality 在 \"明确有对错\" 的场景下更容易影响 judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response\n    质量差异更大更 noisy， style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布\n    不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse， counterfactual\n    rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual\n    quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。 这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific\n    而非 generalizable。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - N_consistent\n    - Formal_WR\n    - Sign_p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - 55\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 48\n      - 56.3%\n      - '0.31'\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - MT-Bench\n      - 42\n      - 52.4%\n      - '0.55'\n    - - Claude\n      - LLMBar\n      - 44\n      - 54.5%\n      - '0.42'\n    - - Claude\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 45\n      - 51.1%\n      - '0.84'\n    - - Claude\n      - MT-Bench\n      - 40\n      - 47.5%\n      - '0.72'\n    - - Gemini\n      - LLMBar\n      - 48\n      - 52.1%\n      - '0.68'\n    - - Gemini\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 46\n      - 50.0%\n      - '0.95'\n    - - Gemini\n      - MT-Bench\n      - 43\n      - 53.5%\n      - '0.49'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: 3×3 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate，颜色编码偏离 50% 程度。仅左上角 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\n    显著着色，其余接近中性灰。'\n  analysis: '9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后 连这一个也不再显著\n    (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果 formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark\n    交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \"benchmark characteristics mediate\n    bias detectability\"，但说服力有限。\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: '对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n    gpt4o_llmbar_gap: significant\n    claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n    claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n    claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.545\n    claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n    claude_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n    gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n    gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.82\n    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.521\n    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.68\n    gemini_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n    n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n    n_combos_both_null: 7\n    n_combos_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。\n    其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \"gap\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的\n    gap 案例可能是 statistical fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert\n    也 显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献 完全瓦解。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - Likert_ATE\n    - Likert_p\n    - Pairwise_WR\n    - Pairwise_p\n    - Gap\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - '-0.10'\n      - '0.33'\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - Pairwise-only\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - '0.04'\n      - '0.71'\n      - 56.3%\n      - '0.31'\n      - Neither\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - MT-Bench\n      - '0.01'\n      - '0.92'\n      - 52.4%\n      - '0.55'\n      - Neither\n    - - Claude\n      - LLMBar\n      - '0.05'\n      - '0.61'\n      - 54.5%\n      - '0.42'\n      - Neither\n    - - Claude\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - '-0.02'\n      - '0.85'\n      - 51.1%\n      - '0.84'\n      - Neither\n    - - Claude\n      - MT-Bench\n      - '0.03'\n      - '0.77'\n      - 47.5%\n      - '0.72'\n      - Neither\n    - - Gemini\n      - LLMBar\n      - '0.02'\n      - '0.82'\n      - 52.1%\n      - '0.68'\n      - Neither\n    - - Gemini\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - '0.00'\n      - '0.99'\n      - 50.0%\n      - '0.95'\n      - Neither\n    - - Gemini\n      - MT-Bench\n      - '0.06'\n      - '0.55'\n      - 53.5%\n      - '0.49'\n      - Neither\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合的 Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value，红线标\n    0.05。仅一个组合的 pairwise 柱低于红线。'\n  analysis: 'C2 的 \"Likert Blindspot\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but pairwise\n    detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被 exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise\n    在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应—— 这更像 \"there is no bias to detect\" 而非 \"Likert misses bias\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Tone axis negative control\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录 epistemic\n    commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n    both_pass_rate: 0.45\n    failure_mode: epistemic commitment change\n    role_in_paper: negative control — axis boundary evidence\n    assertive_nli_mean: 0.656\n    hedging_nli_mean: 0.793\n    catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n  result_rationale: '此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone 作为 negative\n    control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱： working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而\n    formality 又只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\"\n    不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅 作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Method boundary diagram: formality (content-preserving ✅) vs tone (epistemic\n    commitment change ✗) vs verbosity (information-changing ✗)。简单分类图，不需要新数据。'\n  analysis: 'C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\"，\n    贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability window\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\n\n    '\n- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化 original\n    preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.62\n    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.048\n    claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n    claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n    gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n    gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.31\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr: 0.59\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p: 0.12\n    gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr: 0.61\n    gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n    cross_condition_orig_pref_mean: 0.59\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.5\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.48\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge: 0.545\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \"style bias\"。\n    GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好 62%），剩余 formality\n    特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset： 当 original 是 casual（即 formal version\n    是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅 54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality\n    bias 几乎消失。 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)， 在\n    worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset 的 formal win rate\n    在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \"formality bias\" 可能本质上是 \"original text preference + directional\n    confound\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - Orig_pref_WR\n    - Orig_pref_p\n    - Casual-orig_formal_WR\n    - Casual-orig_p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - 62.0%\n      - 0.048*\n      - 54.5%\n      - '0.83'\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 59.0%\n      - '0.12'\n      - 51.2%\n      - '0.91'\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - MT-Bench\n      - 61.0%\n      - '0.06'\n      - 50.0%\n      - '1.00'\n    - - Claude\n      - LLMBar\n      - 58.0%\n      - '0.18'\n      - 50.0%\n      - '1.00'\n    - - Gemini\n      - LLMBar\n      - 56.0%\n      - '0.31'\n      - 48.0%\n      - '0.72'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Decomposition bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate 分解为 original preference\n    component + residual formality component。视觉上显示 residual 接近 0。'\n  analysis: 'Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual\n    formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\"apparent style bias is confounded with\n    original-text preference\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50% win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality\n    和 original preference 方向相反时， formality bias 消失。\n\n    '\n- name: Scaled replication (n=300-500)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。 Power analysis\n    确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_total: 400\n    n_valid_consistent: 220\n    formal_wins: 132\n    casual_wins: 88\n    formal_win_rate: 0.6\n    sign_p: 0.004\n    wilson_ci:\n    - 0.534\n    - 0.663\n    power_at_d02: 0.35\n    power_at_d05: 0.88\n    casual_orig_subset_n: 95\n    casual_orig_formal_wr: 0.516\n    casual_orig_p: 0.67\n    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n    effect_size_cohens_h: 0.2\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1% 下降到\n    60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original subset 在 n≈95 时 formal\n    win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在 控制 original preference 后消失。effect size\n    (Cohen''s h=0.20) 属于 small， 且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power\n    仅 35%——如果真实 效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了 formality 和 original\n    preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\"at scale, the significant overall effect decomposes into\n    original preference + noise\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)'\n    columns:\n    - Subset\n    - N\n    - Formal_WR\n    - Sign_p\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - All consistent\n      - 220\n      - 60.0%\n      - 0.004**\n      - '[0.534, 0.663]'\n    - - Formal-original\n      - 125\n      - 66.4%\n      - 0.001**\n      - '[0.577, 0.742]'\n    - - Casual-original\n      - 95\n      - 51.6%\n      - '0.67'\n      - '[0.415, 0.615]'\n    - - NLI≥0.90\n      - 187\n      - 61.5%\n      - 0.003**\n      - '[0.543, 0.683]'\n  figures_description:\n  - Formal win rate 随 n 增长的 running average plot，标 95% CI band。显示效应从 ~69% 向 ~60% 收敛，且\n    casual-original subset 收敛到 ~50%。\n  analysis: 'n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)； (2) casual-original\n    subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \"original preference confound\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\n\n    '\n- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变 词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n: 100\n    nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n    bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n    joint_pass_rate: 0.48\n    stopped_at: content_verification\n    stop_reason: NLI 72% < 80% threshold\n    academic_to_conversational_nli_mean: 0.81\n    conversational_to_academic_nli_mean: 0.65\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational\n    转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \"our findings demonstrate\" 变成口语\n    \"we found\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的 \"statistically significant correlation\n    (r=0.82, p<0.001)\" 变成口语 \"there''s a pretty strong link\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic\n    方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers, citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72%\n    总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD 方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification'\n    columns:\n    - Direction\n    - N\n    - NLI_mean\n    - NLI≥0.80\n    - BERTScore_mean\n    rows:\n    - - Academic→Conversational\n      - 52\n      - '0.81'\n      - 73%\n      - '0.82'\n    - - Conversational→Academic\n      - 48\n      - '0.65'\n      - 52%\n      - '0.77'\n    - - Overall\n      - 100\n      - '0.72'\n      - 63%\n      - '0.80'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围 收窄到仅 formality——且即使\n    formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。 C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\"we attempted\n    three additional axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.8\n    llama_bertscore_mean: 0.88\n    llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.58\n    llama_sign_p: 0.21\n    qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.691\n    qwen_sign_p: 0.006\n    rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.72\n    nli_correlation_qwen_llama: 0.61\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58%\n    (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting style 不同，Llama\n    可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80% vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对\n    rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本 显著。这引入 \"researcher degrees of freedom\" 质疑——如果换一个\n    rewriter 就不 显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个 rewriter\n    的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check'\n    columns:\n    - Rewriter\n    - NLI_pass\n    - Formal_WR\n    - Sign_p\n    - N_consistent\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - 88%\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - 55\n    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n      - 80%\n      - 58.0%\n      - '0.21'\n      - 50\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: 100 pairs 的 Qwen NLI score vs Llama NLI score，标 0.80 threshold\n    线。显示 moderate correlation 但有 substantial disagreement zone。'\n  analysis: 'rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到 formality\n    bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。 路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\n\n    '\n- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: '对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本， formal\n    version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_pairs: 88\n    formal_higher: 42\n    casual_higher: 26\n    tied: 20\n    n_non_tied: 68\n    binarized_sign_p: 0.032\n    formal_higher_rate: 0.618\n    effect_direction: formal preferred in binarized Likert too\n  result_rationale: '这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04，\n    说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33 不显著是因为 Likert\n    评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise 大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise\n    gap 来自 sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对 小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired\n    t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \"Likert Blindspot\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t\n    检验在 粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise） 都能检测到效应。C2 从 \"measurement\n    method structural advantage\" 坍缩为 \"statistical test choice matters\"——这是 trivially\n    true 且 novelty 极低。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - N_non-tied\n    - Formal_preferred\n    - Preferred_rate\n    - Sign_test_p\n    rows:\n    - - Likert (paired t-test)\n      - 88\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '0.332'\n    - - Likert (binarized sign test)\n      - 68\n      - 42\n      - 61.8%\n      - 0.032*\n    - - Pairwise (sign test)\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n  figures_description:\n  - 三栏对比图：左=Likert paired t-test (NS)，中=Binarized Likert sign test (p=0.032)，右=Pairwise\n    sign test (p=0.006)。视觉化显示 gap 来自 test choice 而非 measurement method。\n  analysis: 'C2 证伪。\"Likert Blindspot\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是： \"Pairwise comparison\n    amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation, but this amplification\n    also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise should be treated as complementary\n    detectors with different sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs。\" 标题改为 \"Sensitivity-Specificity\n    Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias Detection\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\"不同方法有不同检测特性\") 而非 prescriptive\n    (\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\")。\n\n    '\n- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: '测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    threshold_70_n: 82\n    threshold_70_formal_wr: 0.65\n    threshold_70_p: 0.018\n    threshold_75_n: 75\n    threshold_75_formal_wr: 0.67\n    threshold_75_p: 0.012\n    threshold_80_n: 68\n    threshold_80_formal_wr: 0.68\n    threshold_80_p: 0.009\n    threshold_85_n: 58\n    threshold_85_formal_wr: 0.7\n    threshold_85_p: 0.006\n    threshold_90_n: 46\n    threshold_90_formal_wr: 0.74\n    threshold_90_p: 0.002\n    threshold_95_n: 30\n    threshold_95_formal_wr: 0.77\n    threshold_95_p: 0.005\n    monotonic_increase: true\n    critical_finding: higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\n  result_rationale: '结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是 \"方法 robust\"，而是\n    \"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality 是 confound\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是\n    rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version 更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以\n    judge 偏好 formal version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold\n    70% 时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。 这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但\n    worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否 systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity'\n    columns:\n    - Threshold\n    - N_consistent\n    - Formal_WR\n    - Sign_p\n    - Cohen's_h\n    rows:\n    - - '0.70'\n      - 60\n      - 65.0%\n      - '0.018'\n      - '0.31'\n    - - '0.75'\n      - 56\n      - 67.0%\n      - '0.012'\n      - '0.35'\n    - - '0.80'\n      - 52\n      - 68.0%\n      - '0.009'\n      - '0.37'\n    - - '0.85'\n      - 46\n      - 70.0%\n      - '0.006'\n      - '0.41'\n    - - '0.90'\n      - 38\n      - 73.7%\n      - '0.002'\n      - '0.49'\n    - - '0.95'\n      - 26\n      - 76.9%\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.57'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis line chart: x=NLI threshold, left y=formal win rate (上升), right y=n\n    (下降)。显示 sensitivity-sample size tradeoff。'\n  analysis: '结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要 这个实验不显著——它需要的是\n    effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。 路径 B 下这可以作为 \"methodological caveat: NLI\n    filtering may introduce selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: '比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths,\n    task types。零成本 reanalysis。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    consistent_n: 55\n    inconsistent_n: 43\n    discard_rate: 0.439\n    consistent_mean_nli: 0.91\n    inconsistent_mean_nli: 0.87\n    nli_diff_p: 0.08\n    consistent_mean_orig_len: 285\n    inconsistent_mean_orig_len: 342\n    length_diff_p: 0.03\n    consistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.58\n    inconsistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.51\n    task_type_distribution_differs: true\n    chi2_task_type_p: 0.04\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98)\n    相比 inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)； (2)\n    更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长 (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是\n    task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs 过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained\n    pairs 是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否 仅反映了 filter 保留的特定\n    task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被 formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative\n    salience 更高），那 bias 来自 filtering 而非 formality。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check'\n    columns:\n    - Property\n    - Consistent (n=55)\n    - Inconsistent (n=43)\n    - Diff_p\n    rows:\n    - - NLI mean\n      - '0.91'\n      - '0.87'\n      - '0.08'\n    - - Orig text length (chars)\n      - '285'\n      - '342'\n      - 0.03*\n    - - Formal version longer (%)\n      - 58%\n      - 51%\n      - '0.34'\n    - - Task type χ²\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 0.04*\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Box plots: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI score 和 text length 分布对比。'\n  analysis: 'filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了 \"results\n    may be an artifact of data processing choices\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下 需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity\n    analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求 看效应是否持续)。\n\n    '\n- name: Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: '人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。 报告 human-NLI\n    Cohen''s kappa。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_annotated: 80\n    human_pass_rate: 0.74\n    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n    agreement_rate: 0.78\n    cohens_kappa: 0.42\n    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.18\n    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.08\n    human_agrees_formal_better_preserved: true\n    annotation_method: LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false\n    positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs 如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content\n    差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42\n    属于 \"moderate agreement\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline acceptable。GPT-4o\n    作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular\n    validation 风险。20 个 human spot checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - 'Human: Pass'\n    - 'Human: Fail'\n    rows:\n    - - 'NLI: Pass (n=68)'\n      - 56 (TP)\n      - 12 (FP)\n    - - 'NLI: Fail (n=12)'\n      - 3 (FN)\n      - 9 (TN)\n    - - ''\n      - κ = 0.42\n      - ''\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着 ~10 个 consistent\n    pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径\n    B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis excluding human-flagged false positives。\n\n    '\n- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 'Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction\n    作为 predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_observations: 110\n    model_aic: 142.3\n    model_bic: 153.1\n    formality_coef: 0.28\n    formality_coef_se: 0.22\n    formality_coef_p: 0.21\n    original_status_coef: 0.65\n    original_status_coef_se: 0.21\n    original_status_coef_p: 0.002\n    interaction_coef: 0.12\n    interaction_coef_p: 0.58\n    pseudo_r2: 0.06\n    casual_orig_subset_n: 38\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.526\n    casual_orig_sign_p: 0.72\n    formal_orig_subset_n: 50\n    formal_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.78\n    formal_orig_sign_p: 0.001\n    logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.21\n    logistic_original_status_p: 0.002\n  result_rationale: 'worst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status 显著\n    (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects： (1) formality coefficient\n    p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2)\n    original_status coefficient p=0.002—— 是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明\n    original preference 不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是\n    formal 还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6% (p=0.72)——当\n    formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当\n    formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈 偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo\n    R² = 0.06 说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的 statistical backbone：\"formality\n    bias is an artifact of original-text preference\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction'\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - Coefficient\n    - SE\n    - z\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - Intercept\n      - '-0.42'\n      - '0.31'\n      - '-1.35'\n      - '0.18'\n    - - Formality (formal=1)\n      - '0.28'\n      - '0.22'\n      - '1.27'\n      - '0.21'\n    - - Original status (original=1)\n      - '0.65'\n      - '0.21'\n      - '3.10'\n      - 0.002**\n    - - Formality × Original\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.22'\n      - '0.55'\n      - '0.58'\n  - name: 'Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status'\n    columns:\n    - Subset\n    - N\n    - Formal_WR\n    - Sign_p\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Formal is original\n      - 50\n      - 78.0%\n      - 0.001**\n      - Original pref + formality aligned\n    - - Casual is original\n      - 38\n      - 52.6%\n      - '0.72'\n      - Original pref opposes formality → null\n    - - Overall\n      - 88\n      - 64.8%\n      - 0.01*\n      - Confounded aggregate\n  figures_description:\n  - 两组 bar chart：左=formal-original subset (78%, 高), 右=casual-original subset (52.6%,\n    平)。视觉化 formality 效应在控制 original status 后消失。\n  - 'Coefficient forest plot: formality (CI 跨 0), original status (CI 不跨 0), interaction\n    (CI 跨 0)。'\n  analysis: 这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的 \"formality bias\"\n    实际上是 \"original text preference\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此： \"Standard bias detection methods\n    that compare original vs style-transferred text confound style preference with\n    original-text preference。Only the casual-original subset provides an unconfounded\n    estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\" C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\"always\n    control for original status in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset\n    analyses by original direction\"。\n","numLines":916,"startLine":1,"totalLines":916}}}
